- How would you adapt for at-most-k subarrays?
- How would you recover the exact endpoints from the DP table?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with nontrivial segment costs, requiring careful recurrence formulation, efficient range query handling, and solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with fixed number of contiguous segments
- Segment cost computation using range max-min queries
- Reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space optimization techniques

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartitions(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  // Base case: single segment
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    let maxVal = A[0], minVal = A[0];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      maxVal = Math.max(maxVal, A[j]);
      minVal = Math.min(minVal, A[j]);
      dp[i][1] = maxVal - minVal;
    }
  }

  // DP transitions
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const segmentCost = computeCost(A, j + 1, i);
        if (dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost;
          pre[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = pre[end][t] + 1;
    segments.unshift([start, end]);
    end = pre[end][t];
  }

  return { minCost: dp[n][k], segments };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model partitioning with a simple per-block objective and reconstruct optimal cuts. It reveals DP formulation, range queries, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP across two dimensions (prefix and blocks)
- Range maximum precomputation or on-the-fly tracking
- Backpointers for path reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPartitionCostMax(A, m){
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const rangeMax = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let cur = 0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      cur = Math.max(cur, A[j]);
      rangeMax[i][j] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=1;j<=Math.min(i,m);j++){
      for(let t=j-1; t<=i-1; t++){
        const val = dp[t][j-1] + rangeMax[t][i-1];
        if(val < dp[i][j]){
          dp[i][j] = val;
          par[i][j] = t;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, j = m;
  while(j>0){
    const t = par[i][j];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = t;
    j--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][m], partitions: cuts};
}
```

